---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Open Challenge privacy notice — MathGraph" description="How MathGraph receives, safeguards, and retains enquiries for the free-first-finding challenge." currentPath="/assurance/privacy/">
  <header class="section section--compact"><div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">MathGraph · Open Challenge</div>
    <h1>How we handle your enquiry</h1>
    <p class="lede">Submit only the public source and high-level engineering information needed to consider a bounded investigation. Do not include private source, credentials, personal records, confidential business information or undisclosed vulnerabilities.</p>
  </div></header>
  <section class="section section--compact"><div class="shell">
    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <p>We collect the repository URL, the claim or requirement, the decision it supports, what could happen if the claim were false, your description of supporting evidence, your project relationship, and your contact email. If you arrive through a campaign link, we also record limited campaign attribution (source, medium and campaign). We do not provide a source-code upload feature.</p>
    <h2>Purpose and access</h2>
    <p>We use the information solely to evaluate whether to investigate the submitted claim, contact you about the enquiry, and document the enquiry's status. We do not sell submitted information or add you to a marketing list through this form. Submitted records are stored in a private Cloudflare D1 database under the MathGraph owner's Cloudflare account and are not publicly searchable.</p>
    <h2>Bot checks and service providers</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare Turnstile processes the browser verification needed to protect submissions from automated abuse. Cloudflare also hosts the submission endpoint and database. No assurance finding is generated automatically by submitting.</p>
    <h2>Retention and requests</h2>
    <p>Enquiries are subject to a 180-day automated retention limit. You may request earlier correction or deletion by contacting <a href="mailto:heath@mathgraph.org?subject=Open%20Challenge%20privacy%20request">heath@mathgraph.org</a>. We may retain limited information longer if required for a specific legal obligation; otherwise the intake record is deleted by the scheduled retention process.</p>
    <h2>Project authorization and outcomes</h2>
    <p>Submitting an enquiry does not authorize access to a private repository, create a client relationship, guarantee selection, or promise a finding. We arrange any sensitive disclosure and authorization separately. Selected first confirmed findings, if established, are free; further investigation and requalification are separately scoped.</p>
    <p class="fineprint">Notice version: mathgraph-assurance-v1 · 14 November 2026.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button--secondary" href="/assurance/">Return to the Open Challenge</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
